      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, timber operations drew workers to Hartland, supplementing the small ranching communities that had begun forming around scattered homesteads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hartland_california",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hartland hosts the Hartland Christian Camp, a non‑denominational retreat that has hosted summer camps and ministry programs for decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/hartland_california",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community lies near Sequoia National Forest, giving drivers easy access to hiking, camping, and wildlife viewing amid giant sequoia groves.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
